0 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que muchos contratos estén cerca del límite no prueba que haya sido un error o que se haya actuado mal. Puede haber razones legítimas, como necesidades específicas o precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar si los contratos adjudicados en diciembre están relacionados con la misma necesidad. También se puede revisar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 62 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 11.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.9 to 8.3. December accounts for 35% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 22% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,100 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not prove improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases and verify if the same awardee was used for multiple needs. Review the distribution of contracts across different sectors to ensure no single area was over-served.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["8%2B%2FbAWG0tSZ%2FP7lJ7Fu0SA%3D%3D","9u%2F0kR49wOoUqXM96WStVA%3D%3D","1lJGocCxPX1VYjgxA4nMUw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}